    8: /// Document-level gesture surface that owns mouse/touch selection across all
    9: /// editable blocks.
   10: ///
   11: /// Wraps the scrollable editor content. Pointer events are translated to
   12: /// [DocumentPosition]s via the [BlockGeometryRegistry], so a drag that starts
   13: /// in one block can extend the selection into a neighbouring block. This
   14: /// replaces the per-block gesture detectors that previously trapped drags
   15: /// inside a single [TextSelectionSurface].
   16: ///
   17: /// Supports:
   18: /// - tap → place collapsed caret
   19: /// - drag → extend selection (cross-block), with auto-scroll near viewport edges
   20: /// - auto-scroll → every drag (touch or mouse) synchronously scrolls one step
   21: ///   when the pointer enters the viewport edge band, so the list follows the
   22: ///   drag. For mouse/pen, a per-frame [Ticker] *additionally* keeps scrolling
   23: ///   while the pointer is held still near an edge, letting the user scroll
   24: ///   past the visible area. (Touch selection past the viewport uses dedicated
   25: ///   handles, tracked separately as C9.)
   26: /// - double-tap → select word
   27: /// - triple-tap → select block (paragraph)
